    "created_at": "2015-12-23T18:20:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-23T18:20:43Z",
    "body": "Short answer: all the selector `<dfn>`s here just need a `data-noexport` attribute on them.\n\nLong answer: Bikeshed, the major spec-generating tool, builds a dfn database based on a spider that looks at a lot of specs.  By default, \"selector\" definitions are \"exported\", and made available for cross-spec linking in Bikeshedded specs.  This isn't what we want here - those selectors are actually defined in the Selectors spec, and their definitions here are just to provide local anchors for within-spec links, but because they're exported any attempt to autolink to them in Bikeshed is ambiguous and throws an error.  Adding a `data-noexport` attribute tells the spider to mark them as unexported, so they get ignored by default when figuring out cross-spec links, and they'll stop interfering with the Selectors definitions.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
